    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0040" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v21/pg12"/>

                <head>8. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Algeria<anchor n="0" xml:id="d8-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-10-15T18:52:00-04:00">October 15, 1963,
                            6:52 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>609. French Ambassador advised Secretary today<anchor n="1" xml:id="d8-f2"/> that
                        GOF does not intend get involved in
                    Moroccan-Algerian dispute. Possible solutions were direct negotiations between
                    two countries possibly with assist from Tunisia, OAU or UN. He stated Moroccans had
                    advanced to points within Algerian territory as last administered by French,
                    while admitting international border in this region had never been defined.</p>
                <p>Secretary indicated USG would also not wish
                    become involved and would certainly refrain from any initiatives this direction.
                    In view boundary history resort to ICJ would not
                    seem be feasible means for resolution of problem. Therefore Algerian-Moroccan
                    negotiations would appear be only course open.</p>
                <p>Alphand listed as possible Moroccan aims:
                    (1) seizure of limited number of advanced points in preparation for border
                    negotiations, (2) obtaining control of Tindouf and its mineral deposits and
                    possibly (3) positioning for greater pressures on Mauritania.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d8-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d8-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, POL 32-1 ALG-MOR. Confidential.
                    Drafted by Hooper and approved by
                        Williams. Also sent to Rabat and
                    repeated to Paris and Tunis.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d8-f2" n="1" xml:id="d8-f2-content">
                <p>A memorandum of this conversation is ibid.</p>
